<section class="saas-legal-page">
  <div class="saas-container saas-page-shell">
    <div class="saas-page-hero">
      <p class="saas-legal-kicker">Avatar Stickers</p>

      <h1>AI Avatar Sticker Generator</h1>

      <p>
        Turn a portrait or character idea into an avatar-style AI sticker for profiles, chats,
        thumbnails, and social posts.
      </p>

      <a class="saas-button saas-button-primary" href="/?mode=portrait#generator">
        Create Avatar Sticker
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="saas-info-grid">
      <article class="saas-info-panel">
        <h2>Portrait avatar stickers</h2>

        <p>
          Upload a bright, clear portrait to create a stylized sticker avatar from a real face.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="saas-info-panel">
        <h2>Character avatar prompts</h2>

        <p>
          Use text prompts for fictional mascots, creator avatars, team icons, and reaction sticker sets.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="saas-info-panel">
        <h2>Save and reuse</h2>

        <p>
          Favorite the best avatar sticker results, regenerate variations, and download PNG or WebP files.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>How to create an AI avatar sticker</h2>

      <ol>
        <li>
          Upload a portrait for a face-based avatar or write a character prompt from scratch.
        </li>

        <li>
          Use profile-focused words such as avatar sticker, expressive face, and clean outline.
        </li>

        <li>
          Generate variations until the expression, framing, and colors fit your profile use case.
        </li>

        <li>Download PNG for editing or WebP for lightweight social and web profiles.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>Avatar sticker prompt examples</h2>

      <div class="saas-prompt-list">
        <code>creator avatar sticker, friendly smile, clean border, simple background</code>
        <code>
          gaming profile mascot sticker, confident expression, bold outline, neon accent
        </code>
         <code>team icon avatar sticker, cheerful face, rounded shape, crisp sticker style</code>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>Avatar sticker ideas</h2>

      <p>
        AI avatar stickers work for profile pictures, creator branding, community badges, reaction
        packs, team icons, and personal chat stickers. Keep the prompt focused on the face,
        expression, and framing so the result stays readable at small sizes.
      </p>

      <p>
        Use portrait upload when likeness matters, and use text prompts when you want a fictional
        mascot, creator persona, gaming icon, or team character with a consistent style.
      </p>

      <div class="saas-related-links">
        <.link navigate={~p"/face-to-sticker"}>Face to Sticker</.link>
        <.link navigate={~p"/anime-avatar-sticker"}>Anime Avatar Sticker</.link>
        <.link navigate={~p"/custom-sticker-maker"}>Custom Sticker Maker</.link>
        <.link navigate={~p"/sticker-maker-online"}>Sticker Maker Online</.link>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="saas-faq">
      <details open>
        <summary>What is an AI avatar sticker?</summary>

        <p>
          An AI avatar sticker is a profile-style sticker generated from a portrait or character
          prompt, with a readable face, clean outline, and simple sticker framing.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Can I make avatar stickers from text?</summary>

        <p>
          Yes. Use character prompts for creator avatars, mascots, team icons, or reaction stickers
          when you do not want to upload a portrait.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Where do finished avatar stickers go?</summary>

        <p>
          Completed results appear in your sticker history with download, favorite, and regenerate
          options.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
